From 42401f594782e8c8916a16586aedb2f260fb2483 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: p104-k1-builder <k1@z4-p104.local>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 04:00:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/20] p104 k1 v9: review hardening

- clamp the row index so 4-rows-per-block launches never read past the last row (needs nrows_x in the kernel)
- 16-byte alignment check in the wide Q4_K/Q5_K vec_dots, 4-byte load fallback (same math); P104_FORCE_SCALAR_LOADS test hook
- small_k decision uses upstream vdr/nwarps again (threshold back to K < 2048)
- dispatch trace compiled out unless GGML_P104_MMVQ_TRACE is defined; drop dead P104_EXACT_SUM branch
- perf cases for n = 1..3 on the model shapes and K = 2048/2560/3072

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
